# AWCMS — Bahasa Indonesia catalog (ADR-0095).
#
# `nplurals=1`: Bahasa Indonesia does not inflect for number ("satu berkas" /
# "dua berkas"), so every plural message has exactly one form. `PLURAL_FORM_COUNT`
# in `src/lib/i18n/locales.ts` declares the same thing in code, and
# `i18n:catalog:check` asserts the two agree — the `plural=` expression below is
# read to be VERIFIED, never evaluated (ADR-0095 §"Keputusan 2").
#
# TRANSLATION NOTES
#
# - Product and protocol names stay untranslated: AWCMS, ABAC, SEO, MFA, TOTP,
#   sync, cache, outbox. Translating "ABAC policies" to "Kebijakan ABAC" keeps the
#   acronym because that is what the operator reads in the ADRs and the API.
# - "Tenant" is kept as "tenant". It is the domain term throughout this repo's
#   Indonesian documentation and ADRs; "penyewa" would be a second vocabulary for
#   the same concept.
# - Imperative UI verbs use the bare stem Indonesian UI convention ("Simpan",
#   "Keluar") rather than the me- prefix.
msgid ""
msgstr ""
"Project-Id-Version: awcms\n"
"Language: id\n"
"MIME-Version: 1.0\n"
"Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\n"
"Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\n"
"Plural-Forms: nplurals=1; plural=0;\n"

